# 3b Robinhood Agentic — scheduled jobs.
# Install with:  crontab -e   (paste, then verify with:  crontab -l)
#
# Paths are M's real checkout. They contain a SPACE, so every path is quoted and every job is
# invoked through `bash` — cron splits an unquoted command on whitespace and would otherwise run
# "/home/jared-williams/projects/3b." with "Robinhood" as its first argument.

CRON_TZ=America/New_York

# Point the cycle at the PROD compose so `docker compose exec` hits the prod backend container.
# Unquoted on purpose: cron takes an environment value literally to end of line, so the space in
# the path is fine here — unlike in the job command below, which cron DOES split on whitespace.
AGENTIC_COMPOSE_FILE=/home/jared-williams/projects/3b. Robinhood Agentic/deploy/docker-compose.prod.yml

# Only needed if the robinhood MCP is PROJECT-scoped (set it to that project dir). If the MCP is
# added at USER scope (recommended), the cwd doesn't matter — leave this commented out.
# AGENTIC_MCP_CWD=/home/jared-williams/projects

# ── Daily marking: the equity curve ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Syncs the broker mirror, loads the day's closes, then marks the book. 17:15 ET is after the
# 16:00 close with room for the vendor to publish the daily bar. Weekdays only; the job skips
# market holidays itself via market_calendar.
#
# This one is NOT optional if the performance page is meant to mean anything. A missed day is a
# permanent hole: a live mark is refused once it is more than 3 days old and must then be
# backfilled as an explicitly historical mark.
15 17 * * 1-5 /usr/bin/env bash "/home/jared-williams/projects/3b. Robinhood Agentic/bin/nightly_marks.sh"

# ── Twice-daily cycle ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Each run: refresh the snapshot via the Robinhood MCP (host), then run the in-container cycle
# (scan + per-position debates + report). Logs go to logs/cron/<date>-<phase>.log.
#
# NOT INSTALLED on M as of 2026-08-18 — it drives a host-side `claude` invocation through the
# Robinhood MCP, which nobody has run unattended yet. Enable deliberately, not by pasting.
#
# Market OPEN 09:30 ET → run at 09:32 (let the open print settle). Mon–Fri.
# 32 9 * * 1-5 /usr/bin/env bash "/home/jared-williams/projects/3b. Robinhood Agentic/bin/scheduled_cycle.sh" open
#
# Market CLOSE 16:00 ET → run at 16:02. Mon–Fri.
# 2 16 * * 1-5 /usr/bin/env bash "/home/jared-williams/projects/3b. Robinhood Agentic/bin/scheduled_cycle.sh" close
